diagnostics/trailing-block-arguments.em:8:32: the trailing block gives `block` a second value
  each(block: { v => print(v) }) { v =>
                                 ^^^^^^
A block after the parentheses is `block`. Remove `block:` from inside them, or pass the block there instead.
diagnostics/trailing-block-arguments.em:15:1: this call gives `grid` no value for parameter `cell`
  grid(1)
  ^^^^
Pass it as a block after the parentheses, or by name as `cell: ...`.
diagnostics/trailing-block-arguments.em:20:1: `nothing_to_fill` takes 0 arguments, but this call passes 1
  nothing_to_fill() { =>
  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Match the number of arguments to the function's parameters.
diagnostics/trailing-block-arguments.em:27:35: `self.label` is not set yet when this default runs
      constructor(wide: Bool = self.label == "x") {
                                    ^^^^^
A parameter default runs before the constructor's body, so it can read only fields that have defaults of their own.
